Patch 11 -- symmetric entry-38 A/B and a passive shipping-win32u display_lock history.

This is research-only and incremental after patch 10 plus the p68 lower-tail
source described in `MGS2_NATIVE_DRAW_TAIL_AND_DIRECT_MUTEX_2026-08-20.md`.

The A/B half registers a validated guest control block. The displayed-frame
tick publishes route/settle and consumes guest-side counters; the guest control
arm calls its body directly instead of paying high-frequency RunFunctionFmt().

The reliability half observes the exact shipping `win32u_glfuncs3.so` from the
existing pthread wrapper. The frozen 0x6040623c is `display_lock` at RVA
0x20623c, not `session_lock` at RVA 0x226284. The first target match uses the 16
bytes after the exact shipping lock call (return RVA 0xfa4a8), then a bounded
memory ring retains only target ATTEMPT/ACQUIRED/RELEASE events. No hot-thread
logging is added. The public record is deliberately exported for the external
reader and retained when the research binary is stripped.

Regenerate `mgs2_island_entry_identity.h` from the paired p68b DLL after applying
Wine patch 64; entry 38 becomes marker +11 / RVA 0xb9aa0. Regenerate class B from
the same DLL and preserve the already-verified class-C table if the exact mounted
opengl32 DLL is unavailable; do not substitute a different local DLL.

